# ling3-w4a8-gptq.recipe -- Ling-3.0-flash or a fine-tune of it (Ling-3.0-flash-Sante) from the bf16
# checkpoint: the routed experts at four bits, an int4 code and a bf16 scale per 128 of K, chosen by
# GPTQ against the Hessians of a calibration run (docs/MOE-W4.md "Calibration"); everything else as
# the checkpoint holds it. The format is ling3-w4a8-rtn.recipe's, so the same kernels serve both.
#
#   1. rad-convert <checkpoint> --recipe data/recipes/ling3-w4a8-rtn.recipe -o ling3-w4a8-rtn.rad
#   2. RADIANCE_CALIB_DIR=<calib dir> radiance --model ling3-w4a8-rtn.rad ...   (a calibration run:
#      whole experts per rank; push a corpus that looks like the traffic through prefill)
#   3. CALIB=<calib dir> rad-convert <checkpoint> --recipe data/recipes/ling3-w4a8-gptq.recipe \
#          --reuse ling3-w4a8-rtn.rad -o ling3-w4a8-gptq.rad
#
# A routed expert's down projection takes its own Hessian where the calibration routed it enough rows,
# the layer's pooled one otherwise (libquant says which on stderr).
#
# Measured on Ling-3.0-flash-Sante as ling3-w4a8-rtn.recipe is: mean KL 0.036, top-1 agreement
# 92.96%, from 1.26M calibration tokens of medical text, documents, code, tool calls and chat.

blk.*.ffn_*_exps.*.weight  gptq  codes=i4 group=128 scale=bf16 calib=$CALIB
